window.__SEARCH_INDEX__=[{"t":"About me","p":"About me","u":"About/AboutMe.html","x":"Engineer by profession, Educator by passion Hi, I'm Vaisakh. I build multi-domain physical system simulations from first principles, contribute to open-source modeling standards, and break down complex engineering topics into practical tutorials. Whether I’m modeling transient thermal-fluid networks in Modelica, coupling multi-FMU co-simulations, or scripting local-first AI tools in Python, I care deeply about transparent, deterministic engineering over black-box shortcuts. Outside of day-to-day engineering work, I run Simulation Workshop—an educational channel and documentation hub dedicated to helping engineers master multi-domain system modeling—and actively contribute to the Modelica Standard Library ecosystem. ⚙️ System Modeling Thermal-fluid networks, 1D finite volume heat transfer, magnetic circuits, and SSP/FMU co-simulation workflows. 🎥 Simulation Workshop Creating deep-dive video walkthroughs and open documentation that bridge theoretical equations with live OpenModelica code. 🛠️ Open-Source & Local AI Contributing to Modelica libraries and building lightweight Python pipelines and local LLM utilities on Linux. Find me at LinkedIn Checkout on YouTube Find with me on GitHub"},{"t":"Introduction to Modelica Language","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#introduction-to-modelica-language","x":"It is tempting to get started with a new tool by writting something and see the results. But I feel it is important to acknoledge the history and the milestones of its development. This video covers the why and how of Modelica's evolution, the concept of modeling physical systems through equations and an introduction to Open Modelica ecosystem. Introduction to Modelica"},{"t":"Building your first model from scratch - Modelica Basics","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#building-your-first-model-from-scratch-modelica-basics","x":"The first YouTube video."},{"t":"Modelica Standard Library - The power of pre-validated models","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#modelica-standard-library-the-power-of-pre-validated-models","x":"The first YouTube video."},{"t":"Building Your own models and connecting them to to MSL Components","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#building-your-own-models-and-connecting-them-to-to-msl-components","x":"The first YouTube video."},{"t":"Building an Electrical Kettle in Modelica - Introudction to multi-domain simulations","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#building-an-electrical-kettle-in-modelica-introudction-to-multi-domain-simulations","x":"The first YouTube video."},{"t":"Fluid Property Models in Modelica - Thermodynamics in Simulations","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#fluid-property-models-in-modelica-thermodynamics-in-simulations","x":"The first YouTube video."},{"t":"Solving Textbook Problems using Modelica","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#solving-textbook-problems-using-modelica","x":""},{"t":"Modeling a magnetic circuit in Modelica","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#modeling-a-magnetic-circuit-in-modelica","x":"The first YouTube video."},{"t":"Very short Explainers and Tips","p":"Video Tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Video-Tutorials.html#very-short-explainers-and-tips","x":"The first YouTube video. The first YouTube video."},{"t":"Written tutorials on Modelica","p":"Written tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Written-Tutorials.html","x":"title: Installing on Windows description: Step-by-step Windows setup. hide_title: false search: true"},{"t":"Installing on Windows","p":"Written tutorials on Modelica","u":"Modelica-tutorials/Written-Tutorials.html","x":"Content starts here."},{"t":"Quick start","p":"Simulation workshop","u":"index.html#quick-start","x":"This is a very basic Modelica code to simulate the motion of a spring - mass - damper system. Check out more amazing content at the tutorial sections or find out how to get started below. model simpleSpringMass parameter Real M = 5; parameter Real k = 12; parameter Real C = 8; Real x; Real v; initial equation x = 1; equation der(x) = v; M*der(v) + C*v + k*x = 0; annotation( experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 10, Tolerance = 1e-06, Interval = 0.002)); end simpleSpringMass; Are You new to Modelica ? These are the places to check out for more content Modelica Official Website : modelica.org OpenModelica Official Website : openmodelica.org Modelica by Example by Dr. Michael M. Tiller : Modelica by Example OMPython - A python wrapper for OpenModelica compiler :OMPython FMpy - For running FMUs generated from Modelica in python : FMPY Simulation Workshop Youtube Channel : Simulation Workshop"},{"t":"Introduction to System Simulation","p":"Introduction to System Simulation","u":"systemsimulation/Introduction_openModelica.html","x":"Quick Quiz: What is the primary benefit of static site generators? Slower load times Blazing fast speed & high security Requires a heavy database Submit Answer function checkAnswer() { const selected = document.querySelector('input[name=\"q1\"]:checked'); const result = document.getElementById('quiz-result'); if (!selected) { result.style.color = \"orange\"; result.textContent = \"Please select an option first!\"; return; } if (selected.value === \"correct\") { result.style.color = \"green\"; result.textContent = \"Correct! Static sites don't rely on server-side databases.\"; } else { result.style.color = \"red\"; result.textContent = \"Incorrect. Try again!\"; } }"}];